-- title:
--   Both branches meet every supersingular point of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image of the $q$-expansion function field $\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))$ of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ under the coefficientwise map $L((q)) \supseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose $q$-expansion is $q^{-1}$ times the rational $j$-numerator power series, assumed nonzero, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Write $B$ for the $j$-finite chart algebra $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$, i.e. the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y \subset B$ be a prime ideal containing the image of $\varpi$ and supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : B \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathtt{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$: every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $p$. Then every minimal prime of the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $\varpi$ is contained in $y$.
--
--   In geometric terms: the minimal primes over $\varpi$ are the generic points of the components of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$, and the assertion is that every such component passes through each supersingular point of the special fibre. It feeds the subsequent analysis of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ and of the map to $X_0(Mp)$ at supersingular points.
